{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"eb45f9aad585e5ee","name":"card_unit_70th_brigade","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/BloodIron/units/card_unit_70th_brigade","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"70th BRIGADE","text":"At the start of your turn, draw a card and gain +2 HQ defense if this unit was not attacked last turn.","flavorText":"The 70th Infantry Brigade was a brigade of the British Army which participated both in WWI and WWII. The brigade was disbanded in 1919 after WWI, but reformed in 1939 in the Territorial Army. Despite being very poorly trained and equipped, it joined the British Expeditionary Force (BEF) and served in the Battle of France in May 1940, and was then evacuated from Dunkirk. After the ordeal in France the brigade was reformed as an independent formation and redesignated 70th Independent Infantry Brigade. In September it was sent to Iceland where it served as garrison force until December 1941, when it was sent back to the UK to join the 49th Division, nicknamed “The Polar Bears”. The 70th Brigade landed in Normandy on 14 June 1944 as part of the 49th Division where it participated in the Battle of Normandy. In France the brigade saw heavy combat, but withdrew from the frontline in August and disbanded in order to fill the gaps in other infantry formations. In October 1944 the brigade ceased to exist and most of its men were posted to battalions of the 50th (Northumbrian) and the 51st (Highland) Infantry Divisions.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":8},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_70th_brigade","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_70th_brigade_title","SourceString":"70th BRIGADE","LocalizedString":"70th BRIGADE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":1,"defense":8,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_70th_brigade_text","SourceString":"At the start of your turn, draw a card and gain +2 HQ defense if this unit was not attacked last turn.","LocalizedString":"At the start of your turn, draw a card and gain +2 HQ defense if this unit was not attacked last turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_70th_brigade_history","SourceString":"The 70th Infantry Brigade was a brigade of the British Army which participated both in WWI and WWII. The brigade was disbanded in 1919 after WWI, but reformed in 1939 in the Territorial Army. Despite being very poorly trained and equipped, it joined the British Expeditionary Force (BEF) and served in the Battle of France in May 1940, and was then evacuated from Dunkirk. After the ordeal in France the brigade was reformed as an independent formation and redesignated 70th Independent Infantry Brigade. In September it was sent to Iceland where it served as garrison force until December 1941, when it was sent back to the UK to join the 49th Division, nicknamed “The Polar Bears”. The 70th Brigade landed in Normandy on 14 June 1944 as part of the 49th Division where it participated in the Battle of Normandy. In France the brigade saw heavy combat, but withdrew from the frontline in August and disbanded in order to fill the gaps in other infantry formations. In October 1944 the brigade ceased to exist and most of its men were posted to battalions of the 50th (Northumbrian) and the 51st (Highland) Infantry Divisions.","LocalizedString":"The 70th Infantry Brigade was a brigade of the British Army which participated both in WWI and WWII. The brigade was disbanded in 1919 after WWI, but reformed in 1939 in the Territorial Army. Despite being very poorly trained and equipped, it joined the British Expeditionary Force (BEF) and served in the Battle of France in May 1940, and was then evacuated from Dunkirk. After the ordeal in France the brigade was reformed as an independent formation and redesignated 70th Independent Infantry Brigade. In September it was sent to Iceland where it served as garrison force until December 1941, when it was sent back to the UK to join the 49th Division, nicknamed “The Polar Bears”. The 70th Brigade landed in Normandy on 14 June 1944 as part of the 49th Division where it participated in the Battle of Normandy. In France the brigade saw heavy combat, but withdrew from the frontline in August and disbanded in order to fill the gaps in other infantry formations. In October 1944 the brigade ceased to exist and most of its men were posted to battalions of the 50th (Northumbrian) and the 51st (Highland) Infantry Divisions."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnAfterOtherCardAttacks","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"draftBaseWeight":1.1,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Winter_2024/t_bloody_eleventh.t_bloody_eleventh","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Rebellion","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/70th_INFANTRY_BRIGADE.70th_INFANTRY_BRIGADE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":505.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_70th_brigade_photo","SourceString":"Anti-tank gun crew of the 11th Battalion of the 70th Brigade parked alongside a knocked-out German Panther tank, France, June 1944.","LocalizedString":"Anti-tank gun crew of the 11th Battalion of the 70th Brigade parked alongside a knocked-out German Panther tank, France, June 1944."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryL'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryL.47"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeHeavy_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeHeavy.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantr